Icarus Atlas — licensing
========================

This repository holds two different kinds of work, under two different
licenses. Read this section first; it tells you which one applies to what.

  Source code           MIT License (below)
    src/, scripts/, config files, and the build tooling.

  Data and prose        Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
                        International (CC BY-SA 4.0) — see data/LICENSE
    data/ and docs/ — the sourced mythology records, the geographic and
    cultural layers, and the research catalogs. Share-alike is not a
    preference here: part of that material is itself derived from
    CC BY-SA sources and cannot be relicensed.

  Audio                 © 2026 Mehmet Fatih Aksoy. All rights reserved.
    public/audio/*.mp3 — generated by the author with Suno under a paid
    plan. Published here so the atlas runs from a clean checkout; not
    licensed for reuse, redistribution, or derivative works.

  Third-party material  Their own licenses — see ATTRIBUTION.md
    Upstream texts, gazetteers, basemaps, images, and fonts keep the
    licenses their originators granted. ATTRIBUTION.md names every one,
    what was taken from it, and how it is credited.

The ancient source texts the research rests on are NOT redistributed here.
research/corpus/ holds only a manifest of URLs and checksums; the texts
themselves are fetched locally with `pnpm corpus:sync` and are gitignored.


